{"title":"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems\">2007 AMC 12A #1</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">2007 AMC 10A #1</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>One ticket to a show costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/5/555360df10d7f3448442d43c277f763b0d1236bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> at full price. Susan buys 4 tickets using a coupon that gives her a 25% discount. Pam buys 5 tickets using a coupon that gives her a 30% discount. How many more dollars does Pam pay than Susan?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/d/bbd9a3d8b81b9ed86971c0ca7a321cad00202653.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 2\\qquad \\mathrm{(B)}\\ 5\\qquad \\mathrm{(C)}\\ 10\\qquad \\mathrm{(D)}\\ 15\\qquad \\mathrm{(E)}\\ 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"369\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/e/a4e906f85e3a17438d96be998deca8c2d05361c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Answer: \\boxed{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"118\" height=\"32\" /> \nSusan pays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b47260fcc4466689f3d9e25c92eecbdd49b71e82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4)(0.75)(20) = 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" /> dollars. Pam pays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/d/58df5c262098772f3ef75b60ec5ca85f6e6e8c1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5)(0.70)(20) = 70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" /> dollars, so she pays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/8/c188f9e369d611c166a2cb5e7358951c0f82fbfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70-60=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"100\" height=\"13\" /> more dollars than Susan.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A\">2007 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Probl